Opening book
------------
public/data/buku-analisa.json is the ChessClub analysis table derived from
lichess-org/chess-openings, CC0 1.0:
https://github.com/lichess-org/chess-openings
License: public/licenses/chess-openings-CC0.txt.

The Maestro analysis book enriches that table to 27,826 theoretical positions:
scripts/generasi-buku-analisa.mjs replays all 18,713 lines of
public/data/buku-pembukaan.json (the ChessClub opening book, same CC0 source)
and records every position along each line, not just its terminal position.
Pre-existing labels are preserved verbatim; the most-played variant names any
newly covered position.

Puzzles (stored for a future feature, not loaded by the app yet)
----------------------------------------------------------------
public/data/teka-teki.json holds 5,486 mate puzzles copied from ChessClub,
sourced from the Lichess puzzle database, CC0 1.0:
https://database.lichess.org/#puzzles
License: public/licenses/chess-openings-CC0.txt (CC0 1.0 Universal legal code).

public/data/teka-teki-harian/ holds 7,097 daily puzzles (2007-2026) from the
public Chess.com daily puzzle via the samuraitruong/chess.com-daily-puzzle
archive: only dates, FEN positions and solution moves are stored — titles,
authors and media are not taken.
https://www.chess.com/daily-puzzle
https://github.com/samuraitruong/chess.com-daily-puzzle

public/data/teka-teki-video.json holds 6,551 tactics problems (1,681 with
coach discussion videos) using Chess.com puzzle metadata and video links.
